  "implementation": [
    "World captures unit-weight cyclic held metadata, per-view clocks, selected pose snapshots and root identities before activation publication; NPC frustum and selected Player roots choose direct versus captured entry.",
    "World release uses the current active held view and its blend duration, defers unready NI5 or action2 Counter, and preserves passive slot3 ownership. Hard interruption captures resident sources before clearing controller bindings.",
    "Controller restores typed resident tracks, reuses the cache without a new begin, and lets independent native frame retirement disable expired held resources. A real equipment family change interrupts existing typed residence.",
    "Zero-duration refresh and pending LocalScripts OnActive bind existing ownership while deferring control interpretation. This prevents startup defaults from manufacturing a release on a fresh process.",
    "Legacy action6 without typed history retains its prior playback until release; no lost loop history is invented."
  ],
